<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.913 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.913 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.5 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due February 6, 1997 was 2.913 percent, down from 3.193 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.5 billion of 182-day T-bills due May 8, 1997 was 3.067 percent, down from 3.400 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due October 30, 1997 was 3.410 percent, down from 3.681 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$750 million three-month, C$200 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.15 billion of C$7.6 billion of bills due Nov. 14. (Details follow)  </p>
